# Kiosk release packaging

When creating a kiosk Windows build / OTA package / `athena-*.zip` / `Release *.rar`, follow this exact flow.

## Version
1. Bump `apps/kiosk/pubspec.yaml` (`x.y.z+build`), e.g. `0.1.14+15`.
2. Rebuild so the exe product version matches.

## Build
```powershell
$flutter = "C:\Users\Abcom\develop\flutter\bin\flutter.bat"
cd apps\kiosk
& $flutter pub get
& $flutter build windows --release
```
Source folder: `apps/kiosk/build/windows/x64/runner/Release`

## Package layout (must match working `Release pev.rar`)
Archive root must be a single flat folder:

```
Release/
  skp_kiosk.exe
  skp_printer_usb.exe
  *.dll
  data/
```

Hard rules:
- Exactly **one** `skp_kiosk.exe` (reject nested `Release/Release/`).
- Always include **`skp_printer_usb.exe`** beside `skp_kiosk.exe` (copy from last known-good Release if the Flutter build omitted it). Ink/Pages telemetry fails without it.
- Do **not** zip a parent that already contains both `Release/` and `Release/Release/`.

## Outputs
Write to `dist/`:
- `athena-x.y.z.zip` — OTA upload (SHA-256 of this file goes in the release record)
- `Release x.y.z.zip` — same contents
- `Release x.y.z.rar` — **real RAR5** via WinRAR (`Rar.exe`), not a renamed zip
- `athena-x.y.z.sha256.txt` — version, layout, sha256, size

Optional copy: `C:\AthenaOTA\Updates\athena-x.y.z.zip`

## Verify before handing off
```powershell
# zip: one kiosk + one helper, zero nested Release/Release
# rar: 7z must report Type = Rar5
```
